Design note (parity, not scope narrowing):
  The web TagInput is a CONTROLLED, self-contained presentational primitive (value + onChange; data sources
  useTranslation / useAnnouncer / useId / useImperativeHandle). It performs no data fetch, so — exactly like the
  shipped Combobox / CurrencyInput controlled primitives — it has NO loading / async-error / stale / offline chrome.
  Every branch the web source actually renders is reproduced: empty ("No tags yet") vs populated ("Tags: …") chip
  strip, commit on Enter / separator / paste, case-insensitive de-duplication, blocking validator error, at-capacity
  disable + "Maximum N tags" helper, chip removal + Backspace, lower-casing, and the add / "{n} tags added" /
  duplicate / limit-reached / removed announcements. The atomic TsTagInput (Components/Forms/Inputs.cs, backed by
  Core.Forms.TagInputModel) is the separate component-library deliverable and is out of scope per this prompt.

Pre-existing blocker repaired (documented remediation):
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had been concatenated by the .gitattributes
  merge=union strategy into THREE <Project> roots (lines 1 / 1426 / 1427, one carrying a stray BOM) plus duplicate
  Compile ItemGroups — invalid XML (MSB4025 / MSB4067), so `dotnet test` on the solution could not even load the
  project (baseline RED for every surface). Per the file's own header invariant it was regenerated into ONE canonical
  Project root with a single, case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated Compile ItemGroup = the union
  of every Microsoft.UI-free .cs on disk under dashboard-widgets/, feature-views/, misc-surfaces/, modals-dialogs/ and
  shared-surfaces/, plus the new TagInput Model/Source/ViewModel links. Reconciliation verified: 1168 prior distinct
  entries == 1168 disk UI-free files (0 stale, 0 missing); written 1171 entries (1168 + 3 TagInput), 0 duplicates,
  single root, parses as XML. This matches prior repairs (InstallPrompt/0125, SectionErrorBoundary/0138, …).

